abstract: "Proves Xie-Xu Conjecture 4.1 (Electron. J. Combin. 33(4) P4.9, 2026) in a weighted form: for any increasing family generated by singletons and pairs (the dependent sets of a graph with loops) and any nonnegative element weights, k(n-k)A_k^2 >= (k+1)(n-k+1)A_(k-1)A_(k+1). Route: a two-colouring theorem strengthening Horrocks 2000, a marked-downset lemma from Katona's shadow theorem, a critical-element double count, closure under conditioning and the Kahn-Neiman antipodal-pairs criterion. Also proves a weighted Xie-Xu Conjecture 4.4 for additive 2-matroids of rank <= 4 or <= 7 elements (general case open), sharpness examples with triple witnesses, and a variance bound. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text and data CC0-1.0; code MIT."
